WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.247
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Star Breath.

00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:22.494
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:22.494 --> 00:00:26.842
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:26.842 --> 00:00:31.190
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:41.336
This is a breathing practice with a star shape. You will trace a star in the air with one finger — or on your desk, if that feels better. Nothing is drawn and nothing is written. The star lives in the air.

00:00:41.336 --> 00:00:52.931
Here is the shape: as your finger climbs up one point of the star, you breathe in. As your finger comes down the other side, you breathe out. Up, in. Down, out. Five points make one whole star.

00:00:52.931 --> 00:01:05.976
Your finger moves slowly, and your breath follows it. If they fall out of step, that is fine — the breath leads, and the finger catches up. There is no pause at the tip of a point. The breath just turns and flows back down.

00:01:05.976 --> 00:01:11.774
Nothing is ever held. The air moves in, the air moves out. That is the whole shape. Here we go.

00:01:11.774 --> 00:01:24.818
Star one, point one. Finger climbs up… breathing in. Finger comes down… breathing out.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:37.863
Point two. Up… in. Down… out. Slow finger, easy breath.

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:50.907
Point three. Up… in. Down… out. Point four. Up… in. Down… out.

00:01:50.907 --> 00:02:02.503
Point five. Up… in. Down… out. One whole star, finished. Let your hand rest.

00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:03.952
One more star, if you like, on your own — up, in; down, out, all five points. Then let the tracing go, set your hand down, and just breathe the way your body wants to.

00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:16.997
Now hear the rules that keep this practice yours. The star is a gentle guide — it is never a test.

00:02:16.997 --> 00:02:30.041
A smaller star, or a bigger one, is the same practice, whole and complete. Your breath, your pace. And this is never a contest — not the longest, not the quietest, not the slowest, not the biggest.

00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:40.187
And if anything ever feels dizzy, or tight, or strange, the move is simple: breathe normally. Normal breathing is always allowed, at any second. It is never a failure.

00:02:40.187 --> 00:02:41.636
Notice how your breathing feels now, all on its own. Nothing to fix. Nothing to hold.

00:02:41.636 --> 00:02:51.782
Up a point, breathing in. Down, breathing out. Then let it be.

00:02:51.782 --> 00:02:59.029
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:59.029 --> 00:03:04.827
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:03:04.827 --> 00:03:12.074
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:03:12.074 --> 00:03:19.321
You're ready for what's next.
